{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent"],"declarations":55,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.reaches_cycle_observed_unknot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.reaches_cycle_observed_unknot","kind":"theorem","line":561,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L561-L572","doc":"**`reaches_cycle` ⇒ observed output `→` the trivial invariant.** If the\nobservation map assigns the fundamental cycle the unknot value `u`\n(`obs attractor = u`, e.g. the trivial Jones polynomial `tr_M = 1`), then\nevery positive braid-computation in the domain halts to the observed output\n`u`. This is the observational reading of the conjecture: *the halting output\nis the trivial invariant.* ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.reaches_cycle_observed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.reaches_cycle_observed","kind":"theorem","line":551,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L551-L559","doc":"**Observed output stabilises to the attractor's** (conditional on the\nconjecture `reaches_cycle`). For any observation map `obs`, every positive\norbit's observed output eventually equals `obs attractor` — the observed\nhalting output. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SkeinCollatzArith.fundamental_odd_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SkeinCollatzArith.fundamental_odd_step","kind":"theorem","line":531,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L531-L536","doc":"The odd-branch defining equation at `q⁻¹` (the fundamental cycle) follows\nfrom the induced arithmetic whenever `q` is invertible — so the fundamental\n2-cycle is likewise determined by the substrate parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SkeinCollatzArith.coprime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SkeinCollatzArith.coprime","kind":"theorem","line":527,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L527-L529","doc":"**Bézout coprimality** `[3]_q − q·[2]_q = 1` — holds by construction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SkeinCollatzArith.contraction_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SkeinCollatzArith.contraction_gap","kind":"theorem","line":523,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L523-L525","doc":"**Contraction gap** `[2]_q² − [3]_q = q` — holds by construction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SkeinCollatzArith.skein_divisibility","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SkeinCollatzArith.skein_divisibility","kind":"theorem","line":519,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L519-L521","doc":"**Skein divisibility** `[3]_q = q·[2]_q + 1` — holds by construction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SkeinCollatzArith.qi3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SkeinCollatzArith.qi3","kind":"def","line":516,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L516-L517","doc":"Induced `[3]_q = q² + q + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SkeinCollatzArith.qi2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SkeinCollatzArith.qi2","kind":"def","line":513,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L513-L514","doc":"Induced `[2]_q = q + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SkeinCollatzArith.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SkeinCollatzArith.q","kind":"def","line":507,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L507-L507","doc":"The substrate parameter furnished by the QOU. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SkeinCollatzArith.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SkeinCollatzArith.mk","kind":"ctor","line":505,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L505-L505","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SkeinCollatzArith","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SkeinCollatzArith","kind":"structure","line":503,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L503-L507","doc":"The Skein-Collatz arithmetic induced by a substrate parameter `q`\n(a QOU's `q₀`, as an element of the Skein ring `R`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.reaches_cycle_of_descent_domainStable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.reaches_cycle_of_descent_domainStable","kind":"theorem","line":479,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L479-L490","doc":"**Convergence over the domain-stable cone reduces to a descent measure\nalone.** Because `D∞` is forward-invariant, the `hclosed` hypothesis of\n`reaches_cycle_of_descent` is discharged automatically — the open content\nis exactly the existence of the descent measure `μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.domainStable_forward","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.domainStable_forward","kind":"theorem","line":470,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L470-L477","doc":"**The domain-stable cone is forward-invariant**: `C` maps `D∞` into `D∞`\n(unlike the ambient domain, which is not forward-invariant). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.domainStable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.domainStable","kind":"def","line":462,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L462-L468","doc":"The **domain-stable cone** `D∞`: elements whose entire forward orbit stays\nin the domain. This is the well-posed cone for the conjecture — the naive\npositive cone is ill-posed (`C_q` undefined on almost all of it; see\n`pos_domain_stable` and `qcollatz_domain_not_forward_invariant`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.inDomain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.inDomain","kind":"def","line":456,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L456-L460","doc":"The domain of the (partial) Skein-Collatz map: `P` is `q`-even (`[2]_q ∣ P`)\nor `q`-odd (`[2]_q ∣ P + 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.reaches_of_descent_of_forward","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.reaches_of_descent_of_forward","kind":"theorem","line":434,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L434-L454","doc":"**Generic termination-from-descent.** Over any predicate `S` that is\nforward-invariant off `target` and carries a strictly-descending\n`ℕ`-measure, every `S`-element reaches `target`. This is\n`reaches_cycle_of_descent` with the cone abstracted, so it also applies to\nthe domain-stable cone (where forward-invariance is free). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qTwoDvd_oddBranch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qTwoDvd_oddBranch","kind":"theorem","line":421,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L421-L430","doc":"**Odd-branch well-definedness.** When `P` is `q`-odd (`[2]_q ∣ P + 1`), the\nodd-branch numerator `[3]_q·P + 1` is divisible by `[2]_q`, so the odd\nbranch `([3]_q·P + 1)/[2]_q` stays in the Skein ring `ℤ[q]`. Proof: the\nSkein divisibility identity gives `[3]_q·P + 1 = q·[2]_q·P + (P + 1)`, and\n`[2]_q` divides both summands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qTwoValuation_mul_qplus_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qTwoValuation_mul_qplus_one","kind":"theorem","line":409,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L409-L418","doc":"**Even-branch valuation bookkeeping.** Multiplying by `[2]_q = q + 1`\nraises `v_[2]` by exactly one (for `P ≠ 0`); equivalently the even branch\n`P ↦ P/[2]_q` lowers it by one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qTwoValuation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qTwoValuation","kind":"def","line":404,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L404-L406","doc":"The `[2]_q`-adic valuation on `ℤ[q]`: multiplicity of the root `q = -1`\n(equivalently, of the factor `[2]_q = q + 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_laurent_neg_fixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_laurent_neg_fixed","kind":"theorem","line":386,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L386-L391","doc":"**Negative odd-branch fixed point in `ℤ[q^{±1}]`**: `-T(-2) = -(T(-1))²`\nsatisfies `[3]_q·P + 1 = [2]_q·P`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_laurent_fundamental_cycle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_laurent_fundamental_cycle","kind":"theorem","line":376,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L376-L383","doc":"**Fundamental 2-cycle in `ℤ[q^{±1}]`.** The odd branch sends\n`q⁻¹ = T(-1) ↦ 1 + T(-1)` and the even branch sends it back. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_laurent_qunit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_laurent_qunit","kind":"theorem","line":370,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L370-L373","doc":"`T 1` is a unit in `ℤ[T;T⁻¹]` with inverse `T (-1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_attractor_orbit_bounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_attractor_orbit_bounded","kind":"theorem","line":347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L347-L358","doc":"**The fundamental attractor's orbit is a bounded finite invariant set.**\nEvery iterate stays within the 2-cycle `{attractor, C attractor}` — it\nnever escapes. So the attractor is domain-stable (its forward orbit is\na finite invariant set), corroborating that the domain-stable cone is\nnonempty and contains the fundamental cycle `{q⁻¹, 1+q⁻¹}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.iterate_period_two_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.iterate_period_two_mem","kind":"theorem","line":335,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L335-L345","doc":"A period-2 point's forward orbit is exactly `{P, f P}`: every iterate is\n`P` or `f P`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.reaches_cycle_of_descent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.reaches_cycle_of_descent","kind":"theorem","line":301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L301-L333","doc":"**Convergence reduces to a descent measure (proved reduction).**\n\nGiven a QOU's `QCollatz` structure, suppose there is a measure\n`μ : Skein → ℕ` that strictly decreases along the Skein-Collatz map on\nthe positive cone away from the attractor (`hdesc`), and the positive\ncone is forward-invariant there (`hclosed`). Then **every** positive\nelement reaches the fundamental cycle.\n\nThis factors the open conjecture `reaches_cycle` into (i) this proved\ntermination-from-descent lemma and (ii) the existence of such a `μ` —\nthe genuinely open content (the `q`-analog of a Collatz stopping-time\nbound; the paper's `⟨v_[2]⟩ ≥ 2` contact condition is the intended\nwitness). It wires nothing: `μ` is a hypothesis, not supplied. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_domain_not_forward_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_domain_not_forward_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L282-L299","doc":"**Domain non-invariance (concrete counterexample, proved).**\n\nThe Skein-Collatz map is partial: `P` is in its domain iff `P` is\n`q`-even (`φ P = 0`) or `q`-odd (`φ P = -1`), where `φ : R →+* ℤ` is\nthe parity evaluation sending `q ↦ -1` (so `φ [2]_q = 0`). The domain\nis **not** forward-invariant: `[2]_q = q + 1` is `q`-even, its\neven-branch image is `1` (since `1·[2]_q = [2]_q`), yet `φ 1 = 1`, which\nis neither `0` nor `-1` — so `1` has left the domain. This is the\nstructural obstruction with no classical analog (over `ℤ` every element\nis even or odd), backing the `pos_domain_stable` well-posedness field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_qplus1_pow_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_qplus1_pow_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L268-L280","doc":"`[2]_q^k = (q+1)^k ≠ 1` in the Skein ring `ℤ[q]` for `k ≥ 1` (its\n`natDegree` is `k > 0`), discharging the hypothesis of\n`qcollatz_alleven_forces_zero`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_alleven_forces_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_alleven_forces_zero","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L257-L265","doc":"All-even `k`-cycle exclusion: `P = [2]_q^k · P` and `[2]_q^k ≠ 1` in a\ndomain force `P = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_period3_EOO","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_period3_EOO","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L239-L248","doc":"**Period-3, word EOO.** An even→odd→odd 3-cycle forces\n`q·(q³+q²−1)·P₁ = −(q²+2q+2)`. The coefficient `q(q³+q²−1)` is a non-unit in\n`ℤ[q^{±1}]`, so no such `P₁` exists — no EOO 3-cycle. With EEO (and their\nrotations) this excludes every nontrivial period-3 cycle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_period3_EEO","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_period3_EEO","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L230-L237","doc":"**Period-3, word EEO.** An even→even→odd 3-cycle forces\n`q·(q²+2q+2)·P₂ = 1`. Since `q(q²+2q+2)` is a non-unit in `ℤ[q^{±1}]`, no\nsuch `P₂` exists — no EEO 3-cycle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_period2_evenodd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_period2_evenodd","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L213-L221","doc":"**Period-2, word EO/OE.** An even→odd 2-cycle (`P₁·[2]_q = P`,\n`P·[2]_q = [3]_q·P₁ + 1`) forces `q·P₁ = 1`, i.e. `P₁ = q⁻¹` — the\nfundamental cycle `{q⁻¹, 1+q⁻¹}`, uniquely. Together with the EE and OO\ncases, the only positive period-2 cycle is the fundamental one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_period2_oddodd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_period2_oddodd","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L204-L211","doc":"**Period-2, word OO.** An odd→odd 2-cycle forces\n`(q²+2q+2)·(P − P₁) = 0`, hence `P = P₁` in a domain — it degenerates to\nthe odd fixed point `-q⁻²`, not a genuine 2-cycle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_period2_eveneven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_period2_eveneven","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L197-L202","doc":"**Period-2, word EE.** An even→even 2-cycle forces `q·(q+2)·P = 0`,\nhence `P = 0` in a domain (`q ≠ 0`, `q ≠ -2`): no positive EE 2-cycle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_even_fixed_point","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_even_fixed_point","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L179-L187","doc":"**Even-branch fixed points force `q·P = 0`.** A fixed point of the even\nbranch (`[2]_q·P = P`) forces `q·P = 0`, hence `P = 0` when `q` is a\nnon-zero-divisor (as in `ℤ[q^{±1}]`). Together with\n`qcollatz_odd_fixed_point`, the only fixed points of the Skein-Collatz\nmap are `0` (even) and `-q⁻²` (odd) — **neither positive** — completing\nthe period-1 case of nontrivial-cycle exclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_neg_qinv_sq_is_odd_fixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_neg_qinv_sq_is_odd_fixed","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L170-L177","doc":"The negative element `-q⁻²` is an odd-branch fixed point (given `q`\ninvertible): `[3]_q·(-q⁻²) + 1 = [2]_q·(-q⁻²)`. With\n`qcollatz_odd_fixed_point` this identifies `-q⁻²` as *the* odd fixed\npoint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_odd_fixed_point","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_odd_fixed_point","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L159-L168","doc":"**Odd-branch fixed points are pinned by `q²·P = -1`.** A fixed point of\nthe odd branch (`[3]_q·P + 1 = [2]_q·P`) forces `q²·P = -1`, hence\n`P = -q⁻²` once `q` is invertible — the `q`-lift of the classical\nnegative fixed point `-1`. In particular the fixed point is unique and\n*negative*: there is **no positive fixed point**, so the fundamental\n`{q⁻¹, 1+q⁻¹}` is genuinely 2-periodic. This discharges the period-1\ncase of nontrivial-cycle exclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_fundamental_even_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_fundamental_even_step","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L153-L157","doc":"Even-branch step of the fundamental cycle: `q⁻¹·[2]_q = 1 + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_fundamental_odd_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_fundamental_odd_step","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L147-L151","doc":"Odd-branch step of the fundamental cycle: `(1 + q⁻¹)·[2]_q = [3]_q·q⁻¹ + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qi3_sub_q_qi2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qi3_sub_q_qi2","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L120-L131","doc":"**Skein-Bézout coprimality**, derived sorry-free from the class\nfields: `[3]_q - q * [2]_q = 1`.\n\nThis is the engine of the *no-cycles* half of the conjecture: it\nexhibits `[2]_q` and `[3]_q` as coprime (`gcd = 1` by Bézout), so\n`[3]_q^{k_odd} = [2]_q^k` is impossible for `k_odd ≥ 1` and the only\nperiodic orbit is `P = 1`. Its derivability is evidence that the\n`QCollatz` class content is genuine, not a vacuous marker. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.reaches_cycle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.reaches_cycle","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L118-L118","doc":"**The $q$-Collatz conjecture (within the QOU).** Every element of\nthe (domain-stable) positive cone reaches the fundamental cycle —\ni.e. reaches `attractor` — under finitely many iterations of the\nSkein-Collatz map. The `sorry`-free absence of an instance is the\nhonest \"open\" state per §3b-tax. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.pos_domain_stable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.pos_domain_stable","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L111-L111","doc":"**Domain-stability of the positive cone (well-posedness).** The\nSkein-Collatz map is *partial*: it is defined at `P` only when `P`\nis `q`-even (`[2]_q ∣ P`) or `q`-odd (`[2]_q ∣ P + 1`). Unlike the\nintegers — where every element is even or odd — this domain is\n**not** forward-invariant on the naive positive cone: almost every\npositive Laurent element leaves it within a few steps\n(computations/qcollatz_divergence_probe: 6042/6045 escape, most in\none step). So the conjecture's cone `pos` is the **domain-stable**\nsubset — elements whose entire forward orbit stays in the domain.\nThis field records that requirement; it has no classical analog. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.attractor_not_fixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.attractor_not_fixed","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L100-L100","doc":"…and not a fixed point (the fundamental cycle is truly 2-periodic). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.attractor_period_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.attractor_period_two","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L98-L98","doc":"`attractor` is a genuine period-2 point of the Skein-Collatz map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.attractor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.attractor","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L96-L96","doc":"The fundamental attractor `α ∈ Skein` — the `q⁻¹` end of the\nperiod-2 cycle `{q⁻¹, 1 + q⁻¹}` (the `q`-lift of the classical\n`{1, 2}`). The literal ring element `1` is **not** the attractor:\nit is outside the domain of `C`, being neither `q`-even nor\n`q`-odd (`1` reduces to `1 ∉ {0, -1}` modulo `[2]_q`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.pos","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L90-L90","doc":"The positive cone `ℤ[q^{±1}]_{>0}` (archimedean positivity at\n`q > 1`, abstracted). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.C_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.C_odd","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L87-L87","doc":"**Odd branch.** For `q`-odd `P` (i.e. `[2]_q ∣ P + 1`),\n`C P = ([3]_q * P + 1) / [2]_q`, characterised by\n`C P * [2]_q = [3]_q * P + 1`. Well-defined by Skein divisibility\n`[3]_q = q * [2]_q + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.C_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.C_even","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L82-L82","doc":"**Even branch.** For `q`-even `P` (i.e. `[2]_q ∣ P`),\n`C P = P / [2]_q`, characterised by `C P * [2]_q = P`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.C","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.C","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L79-L79","doc":"The Skein-Collatz map `C_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.qi3_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.qi3_def","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L77-L77","doc":"`[3]_q = q^2 + q + 1` (combinatorial convention). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.qi2_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.qi2_def","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L75-L75","doc":"`[2]_q = q + 1` (combinatorial convention). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.qi3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.qi3","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L73-L73","doc":"The $q$-integer `[3]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.qi2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.qi2","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L71-L71","doc":"The $q$-integer `[2]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.qgen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.qgen","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L69-L69","doc":"Image of the formal substrate parameter `q` in the Skein ring\n(a model of $\\mathbb{Z}[q^{\\pm 1}]$). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz.mk","kind":"ctor","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz","kind":"class","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QCollatz.lean#L59-L118","doc":"The $q$-Collatz conjecture: Skein-module crossing resolution.\n\nConjectural class furnished by a QOU — see\n[`conj:q-collatz`](../../../quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/q-collatz-conjecture.md).\nThe `reaches_cycle` field is the open conjecture; the class carries\nthe full definitional content of the Skein-Collatz map. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:q-collatz","label":"conj:q-collatz","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/q-collatz-conjecture.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}